# Versioning

## Semantic Versioning

```
MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH

1.0.0  → breaking changes, major redesign
0.2.0  → new features, backward-compatible
0.1.1  → bug fixes, patches
```

## When to Bump

| Change | Bump | Example |
|--------|------|---------|
| New screen/page | minor | `feat: add drafts page` |
| New feature in existing screen | minor | `feat(chat): add forwarding` |
| Bug fix | patch | `fix: correct unread count` |
| Performance improvement | patch | `perf: virtualize message list` |
| Dependency update | patch | `chore: update React to 19.1` |
| Breaking API/data change | major | `feat!: change store format` |
| i18n: add new language | minor | `feat(i18n): add German` |
| New theme palette | minor | `feat(theme): add green palette` |

## Release Process (Lerna fixed mode)

```bash
# 1. Bump root (.) + all packages/* + lerna.json via Lerna
npm run version:bump -- patch    # or minor, major, or explicit 1.2.3

# 2. Update CHANGELOG.md manually (if needed)

# 3. Commit → MR to master (direct push to master forbidden)
git add -A
git commit -m "chore: release v$(npm run version:print -s)"

# 4. After merge, on master: tag and push tag only (no "v" prefix)
npm run version:tag
```

`npm run version:print` prints the current version from `lerna.json`.

Pushing a semver tag triggers GitHub Actions (`build-electron` + GitHub Release). Push to `master` alone does not create a Release.

## Version is used in

| Where | How |
|-------|-----|
| `lerna.json` | Fixed monorepo version (source of truth) |
| `package.json` (root `.` + all `packages/*`) | `version` field (bumped by Lerna) |
| Electron auto-updater | reads from package.json |
| Sentry releases | `VITE_APP_VERSION` (CI sets from git tag) |
| CHANGELOG.md | manual release notes |
| PWA cache | Workbox precache manifest changes |
| About screen (planned) | `brand.appName + version` |

## Monorepo sync

Lerna `packages: [".", "packages/*"]` + `forcePublish: true` bumps root and every leaf on each release. `lerna run` ignores root (`workspace`) to avoid script recursion.
